# Fault W-B-2: a `partial` sum with one hole term dropped its known terms (`sum(…) partial` printed `?x[b]`).
# L §5.18 Partial answers: "A line marked `partial` prints, when its value is a hole, its known part and the named holes
# it is linear in, each with its coefficient: sums, differences ..." x[a] = 5 is known, x[b] is the hole: the sum is
# 5 + 1 × the hole (s), and less 1 it is 4 + 1 × the hole (t).
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source src "a source"

index ks = [a, b]

input x[k in ks]: int question "x?"

version v
  cite src
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  x[a] = 5 "row"

ask s: sum(x[k] for k in ks) partial

ask t: sum(x[k] for k in ks) - 1 partial
=== expect
s: 5 + 1 × ?"x?" (x[b])
  cut 2026-01-01
t: 4 + 1 × ?"x?" (x[b])
  cut 2026-01-01
